  "body": "Ports the image rendering fixes from the touch work:\r\n\r\n- **Single FAST refresh for image pages**: replaces the blank + double-FAST workaround, straight into the gray pass (keeps the #2190 next-page HALF cleanup)\r\n- **Image size validation overflow**: 64-bit multiply so malformed headers can't bypass the check; cap raised 3MP to 8MP for real ebook covers; decode callbacks yield periodically to keep the watchdog fed\r\n- **Top margin clamp**: full-viewport-height images no longer overflow the page bottom and fail bounds checks (section cache bumped to v38, forces re-index)\r\n- Viewable bezel insets now come from `BoardConfig::ACTIVE.viewableInsets` instead of hardcoded constants (same 9/3/3/3 defaults, no X4 behavior change)\r\n\r\n# EPUB image rendering performance\r\n\r\nMeasured on an Xteink X4 with `Artemis_minimized.epub`. Each cold page contains two JPEGs and starts without extracted image or `.pxc` caches. \r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\n| Metric | Original | Bulk writes, 4 KB chunks | Current, 8 KB chunks | Change, original to current |\r\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| Two cold image pages, total | 81,993 ms | 41,008 ms | 35,226 ms | **-57.0%** |\r\n| ZIP extraction, four images | 56,391 ms | 15,560 ms | 13,869 ms | **-75.4%** |\r\n| JPEG decode/cache, four images | 17,222 ms | 17,074 ms | 17,226 ms | approximately unchanged |\r\n| Display and gray waveforms, two pages | 6,627 ms | 6,619 ms | 2,388 ms | **-64.0%** |\r\n| Estimated image-file SD writes | approximately 4,023,227 one-byte calls | approximately 985 bulk calls | approximately 493 bulk calls | **approximately 99.99% fewer calls** |\r\n| Final display activations after decode | 2 per page | 2 per page | 1 per page | **-50%** |\r\n\r\nThe write-call counts are calculated from the four inflated image sizes (4,023,227 bytes total). Actual ZIP output boundaries can add a small number of partial writes, so the 4 KB and 8 KB figures are estimates rather than instrumented call counts.\r\n\r\n## Per-image cold-path timings\r\n\r\n| Image | Inflated bytes | Original extraction | 4 KB bulk extraction | 8 KB bulk extraction | Original to current | Current JPEG decode/cache |\r\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| `img_0_0.jpg` | 1,259,193 | 17,627 ms | 4,889 ms | 4,317 ms | **-75.5%** | 5,438 ms |\r\n| `img_0_1.jpg` | 833,349 | 11,716 ms | 3,235 ms | 2,865 ms | **-75.5%** | 3,382 ms |\r\n| `img_0_2.jpg` | 901,692 | 12,609 ms | 3,457 ms | 3,139 ms | **-75.1%** | 4,224 ms |\r\n| `img_0_3.jpg` | 1,028,993 | 14,439 ms | 3,979 ms | 3,548 ms | **-75.4%** | 4,182 ms |\r\n\r\n## Per-page totals\r\n\r\n| Cold page | Original | Bulk writes with gray overlay | Current | Original to current |\r\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| `img_0_0` + `img_0_1` | 42,332 ms | 21,059 ms | 18,684 ms | **-55.9%** |\r\n| `img_0_2` + `img_0_3` | 39,661 ms | 19,949 ms | 16,542 ms | **-58.3%** |\r\n\r\nThe current first page used the scheduled HALF refresh (1,723 ms panel wait); the next page used FAST (506 ms). Image pages now participate in the normal refresh cadence instead of forcing every page through HALF followed by a separate grayscale activation.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\n1. `HalFile` now overrides `Print::write(const uint8_t*, size_t)`. Previously, virtual dispatch fell back to Print's byte loop, turning a four-megabyte extraction into roughly four million mutex-protected SD writes.\r\n2. Lazy image extraction now streams 8 KB chunks rather than 4 KB chunks.\r\n\r\n## Remaining cold-path cost\r\n\r\nThe JPEG decoder still accounts for about 17.2 seconds across the four images, essentially unchanged by the storage fixes. Those decodes happen only while creating the `.pxc` cache. Once cached, the measured two-image page turn was 935 ms, including a 506 ms FAST panel refresh.\r\n",
